  "chain": "corrosion bonding between pilot disc and in-body seat [cause B] -> elevated first-lift pressure required to break bond -> SRV pilot assemblies (S/N 378, S/N 376) lift outside TS SR 3.4.3.1 +/-3% tolerance on first actuation -> condition prohibited by Technical Specifications / could have prevented fulfillment of safety function (engineering analysis found no exceedance of overpressure protection or core thermal limits)",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Two SRV pilot assemblies (S/N 378 and 376) independently failed their first-lift TS acceptance criteria due to the same known corrosion-bonding mechanism; modeled as parallel failure chains sharing the same Cause node per rule 5. Subsequent lifts (2nd-4th) for both assemblies were within tolerance, consistent with the known 'bond breaks after initial lift' phenomenon described in Background. No loss of safety function was determined per licensee's Engineering Report; this is reflected in the Consequence description rather than as a separate node. Numerous previous similar occurrences (2007, 2008, 2010, 2011, 2015x2, 2017) are modeled as stub LERs per rule 9, using the LER numbers exactly as stated in the narrative."
}